bitda":4.3810061852170135,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":false,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":0.0,"_gate_accruals":-0.015776467943056257,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":27.2,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.21979145685423182,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":51.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.17989406232590963,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.07833972188558777,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":2.3154404322619144,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.02550214134964854,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":24.8,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.04001121076201419,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":5.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.06421857381245877,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":57.1,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.02961934578248555,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":44.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.029756719253856145,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":12.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.036457654369269545,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":39.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.0094099995,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"InvenTrust Properties Corp. is a premier Sun Belt, multi-tenant essential retail REIT that owns, leases, redevelops, acquires and manages grocery-anchored neighborhood and community centers as well as high-quality power centers that often have a grocery component. Management pursues the Company's business strategy by acquiring retail properties in Sun Belt markets, opportunistically disposing of retail properties, and maintaining a flexible capital structure. A trusted, local operator bringing real estate expertise to its tenant relationships, IVT has built a strong reputation with market participants across its portfolio. InvenTrust Properties Corp. was established on 4th October, 2004 and is incorporated in Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel Joseph Busch | CEO, President & Director | Age 43 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 103 people. Revenue per employee of $2.9M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue falling 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $1.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $106K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["InvenTrust Properties Corp. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $2.5B market cap on $299M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and -4% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at -0% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $111M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 37 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Price sits 18% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.18199676271614626},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(IVT) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutional Tactics","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/IVT_as_a_Liquidity_Pulse_for_Institutional_Tactics_111226022201_1794468121.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794468121.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Raised Guidance Might Change The Bull Case For InvenTrust Properties Stock (IVT)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stock